commit 7f3e9c68a733108f728e1a5e7d516e8179332108
Author: Luke <luke@bermont.digital>
Date:   Fri May 29 10:32:57 2026 +0200

    feat(cache): split persistent-memory so stable profile rides the shared base

    dream-memory's <persistent-memory> profile/** snapshot was trapped at the tail
    of the per-cwd dynamic system-prompt block, so it only cached within the same
    cwd. Move the stable global profile into the cross-cwd cacheable base.

    - harness-cli: dispatchSessionStart returns only volatile per-cwd memory
      (project/<slug> + repowise); profile no longer bundled here.
    - extension: new systemPrompt:build filter (pi-dream-memory.profile-base,
      priority 10) injects profile as the first <project_instructions> block inside
      <project_context>, so cache-base-prompt's extendBase (priority 90) relocates
      it above SYSTEM_PROMPT_DYNAMIC_BOUNDARY into the shared base (when
      PI_EXTEND_BASE_PROMPT=1; harmless tail-lead when off). Profile memoised per
      process for byte-stability; frozen child prompts discard filter output (no
      leak); unsafe content falls back to the tail (no content loss).
    - No bridge change, no cache-base-prompt change required.
    - Eval: profile-base-cache.spec.ts proves byte-stable profile base across two
      cwds + no content loss + extendBase interaction; wired into
      test:dream-memory:cache. Updated 3 specs to the volatile-only contract.

    Verified against a live opus-4-8 bridge dump: persistent-memory is appended to
    event.systemPrompt (not a separate user message) and inbox is excluded from
    SessionStart, correcting the original brief's premise.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 535df7dae560

